Subject: [PATCH 1/2] UFH-12 Phase 0 (PROPOSED, unsigned): declared embedder
 placement + -c 2048; stale lineup text

STACK-CHANGE PACKAGE CONTENT, NOT APPLIED. Awaits the operator signature in
epyc-root artifacts/operator/stack-change-ufh12-phase0-20260926/PACKAGE.md.

A. Embedder placement (REPL-EMB-0.1, operator decision D1 2026-09-26)
- launch_manifest embedding.placement: one cpuset per port on SMT siblings,
  next to each serving model: 8090/8091 node1 136-143 (half A), 8092/8093
  node2 144-151 (half B), 8094/8095 node3 176-183 (GPU host lane). Warm
  8096 (Granite-97M-R2, NOT switched) gets 152-167.
- pool_recipe: context_tokens 512 to 2048 (512 tokens/slot = BGE window),
  no_mmap: true so the membind is real.
- stack_manifest: EMBEDDING_PLACEMENT + import-time validator (every pool
  port declared, one NPS4 node each, -t equals cpuset size, SMT-fold-disjoint
  from each other, the speech cpusets and the GPU host lane).
- orchestrator_stack: declared embedders spawn under
  numactl --membind=<node> + taskset -c <cpuset>; the bench guard may
  refuse, never re-pin. --no-mmap emitted when the recipe asks.
- scripts/server/embedder_affinity_check.py: read-only serving proof from
  /proc (per-task Cpus_allowed_list, OMP places, pool disjointness,
  numa_maps locality, argv vs recipe).

Root cause, read from /proc 2026-09-26: no placement plus OMP_PROC_BIND=spread
OMP_PLACES=cores put all six servers' compute teams on the same places
0/96 32/128 48/144 88/184.

B. Stale comment text (no behaviour): launch_manifest port_map quarters to
halves 8080/8180, Qwen3.6-27B to Qwen3.8-27B (since 2026-08-20), critic
122B to Qwen3.8-Flash-Next UD-IQ4_XS (since 2026-09-22); stack_topology
frontdoor and critic headers + W1 cutover note likewise.

Tests: tests/unit/test_embedding_placement.py (new) + launch-parity file;
302 passed on the affected suites. test_quarter_stack_smoke
test_derived_chat_ports_drop_retired_ports_and_pick_up_live_ones fails
identically on pristine origin/main (pre-existing, KeyError worker_general).

